  <prompt>Build design §5.2 option B: CorrectionRequest gains Note (line and header routes), checked per design §1.1 before any read; CorrectAsync writes sprk_note on each sprk_invoicecorrection row it creates in that call, in the same create. The note is not part of the row's derived id. No Decision Record and no writer change.</prompt>

  <goal>A reviewer's correct or confirm can carry a short note stored with the correction row.</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="EB-D-242">The derived row id is unchanged (a repeat with an edited note finds the same row and does not rewrite the note); no Decision Record.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-64">Correction labels (Corrected, Confirmed individually, Accepted in bulk) are unchanged; Accepted in bulk carries no note.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design 1.1">The shared 400 codes ebilling.note_too_long and ebilling.note_invalid_characters.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No live call. Never run python. Never --no-verify. No bare git stash.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A note is written on every row created by the call; no note writes no sprk_note; the row ids equal the pre-change ids (must-not-fire on an id change).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Bulk accepted rows carry no note; the validation set of 2a.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build --warnaserror 0 warnings; correction suites green; ArchTests green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute for rigor, checkpoints and quality gates.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
